 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a18-v02",
  "song": "tsa-a18",
  "verse": 2,
  "quick_english": "Having handed over his own authority, a teacher who performs no initiation incurs no fault; but before that, by fault, by authority-bond, by the Vidyeśa-state-giving one, bondage itself is his non-performance of initiation. So consecrated, for mantra-deity-identity success, six-monthly, daily, by muttering-fire-offering-special-worship conduct, let him do the knowledge-vow. Thereafter, having attained being-made-of-that, he is entitled in initiation and the rest. Therein: the unfit let him not initiate, nor let him shun the fit; even the initiated let him test in knowledge-giving; knowing even deceit-grasped knowledge, let him overlook it; and herein, by consecration-splendor, god-worship and the rest.",
  "quick_english_source": "manual",
